{"data": [{"broadcast_id": "AvZr6QdT5x", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-30", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 919512, "segment_id": "vqrId2aoHr", "segment_broadcast_id": "AvZr6QdT5x", "segment_title": "Preview/Introduction Brian Williams (New York)", "segment_description": null, "segment_duration": 50, "segment_type_id": 1, "segment_start_time": "63000.0", "legacy_segment_id": 919512, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Preview", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "AvZr6QdT5x", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-30", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 919512, "segment_id": "0toVmmeZlC", "segment_broadcast_id": "AvZr6QdT5x", "segment_title": "Economy: Bailout Bill /Small Businesses", "segment_description": "(Studio: Brian Williams) Report introduced.  \n\n(Capitol: Tom Costello) Talks aimed at reviving the defeated economic bailout bill featured; details given of the stock market rebound, the push for an accounting rule change and the FDIC\u2019s proposal to raise insurance caps for bank deposits; yesterday\u2019s House vote count cited. [President BUSH \u2013 says this is not the end of the legislative process.] [Senator Mitch McCONNELL&#134;- says we\u2019ll get the job done this week.] [Representatives Mac THORNBERRY&#134;, John DUNCAN&#134;, Diana DEGETTE&#134;, Jim LANGEVIN&#134;- comment on the bailout bill.] [Former FDIC chairman Bill ISAAC&#134;- says this is a manufactured crisis.]  \n\n(Studio: Brian Williams) Report introduced.  \n\n(Miami: Mark Potter) The impact of the economic downturn and credit crunch on small businesses featured. [Village Hat Shop Fred BELINSKY&#134;, Miami marketing firm owner Suzanne McDOWELL&#135;, Auto Nation CEO Mike JACKSON&#134;, T&M Technology Solutions, Inc. Mario CIPRIANO&#134;&#134;- describe their struggles to stay in business, get credit and loans and hire new workers.] [National Small Business Assn. MAN \u2013 says they\u2019re facing having to let people go and close their business.] ", "segment_duration": 340, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63050.0", "legacy_segment_id": 919513, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "AvZr6QdT5x", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-30", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 919512, "segment_id": "hEzTClMGR9", "segment_broadcast_id": "AvZr6QdT5x", "segment_title": "Decision 2008 / Obama vs. McCain", "segment_description": "(Studio: Brian Williams) Report introduced.   (Washington: Andrea Mitchell) The presidential race between Senators Barack Obama and John McCain featured; attack ads shown; details given of their views on the economic bailout. [OBAMA, McCAIN \u2013 push for a bailout package.] [McCAIN \u2013 says the Treasury has money to start without Congressional authority.] [OBAMA \u2013 indicates McCain has not focused on getting the job done.] This week\u2019s debate between the vice presidential candidates Governor Sarah Palin, who went to McCain\u2019s Arizona ranch to work with experts, and Senator Joe Biden, who has a reputation for talking too much, noted. [In CBS interview, PALIN \u2013 rambles about the bailout, healthcare reform and job creation.] ", "segment_duration": 140, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63390.0", "legacy_segment_id": 919514, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "AvZr6QdT5x", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-30", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 919512, "segment_id": "V55O1S4dDb", "segment_broadcast_id": "AvZr6QdT5x", "segment_title": "Gasoline Shortage / Southeast", "segment_description": "(Studio: Brian Williams) Report introduced.   (Atlanta: Michelle Kosinski) The gas shortage in the Southeast examined; scenes shown of gas lines and upset drivers; details given of hurricane-related problems, decreased demand due to higher prices and panic buying; statistics on refinery supply cited; pipeline map shown. [Energy analyst John KILDUFF&#134;- notes refineries had no incentive to make or store gasoline.] [American Petroleum Institute Rayola DOUGHER&#134;- talks logistics.] [Gas supplier Tex PITFIELD&#134;&#134;- wonders when we will look at alternative forms.] [AAA Tom CROSBY&#134;- says people need to be patient.] ", "segment_duration": 140, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63530.0", "legacy_segment_id": 919515, "network_name": "NBC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "AvZr6QdT5x", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-30", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 3, "distributor": 10, "broadcast_title": "NBC Nightly News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 919512, "segme